          Sometimes, partly, and with no guarantee. In the best-known lab comparison, vinegar slowed one common indoor mold and had no measurable effect on another, and no grocery-store vinegar is registered with the EPA to kill mold. It is a fine cleaner for light mildew on tile and glass. For wood, drywall, basements or anything that keeps coming back, use a registered fungicide and fix the humidity.
